    ],
    "binSource": "bundled",
    "dummyEnv": {
      "RIPPLING_API_TOKEN": "x-engrams-managed"
    },
    "credentialDelivery": "inject",
    "doc": "Use `rippling` to read your Rippling HR system from this session: workers and their managers, users, departments, teams, locations, titles and levels, employment types, legal entities, leave, time, devices, worker changes, and the activity log, plus custom objects, reports, and the writes Rippling exposes. Authentication is automatic: the egress proxy injects the organization's API token as `Authorization: Bearer` on requests to rest.ripplingapis.com; `RIPPLING_API_TOKEN` is a managed placeholder. Do NOT set a real token or run any login. A path your profile did not grant is denied at the network boundary, not authenticated. Fields the token is not entitled to come back redacted and are listed under `__meta.redacted_fields`.\n\nList commands follow every page (limit 100, cursor) and print one JSON array. Filters use Rippling's syntax: `filter=status eq 'ACTIVE'`, `filter=updated_at gt '2026-10-01T00:00:00Z'`, operators eq ne gt gte lt lte in and or; `expand=user,manager` embeds related records (depth 2); `order_by=start_date`.\n\nCommands and the power each needs:\n  rippling me                                     The caller's own user (company:read)\n  rippling company | rippling legal-entities      The company and its legal entities (company:read)\n  rippling workers [field=value ...]              Workers; filter=, expand=, order_by= (workers:read)\n  rippling worker <id>                            One worker with user and manager embedded (workers:read)\n  rippling worker-by-email <email>                The worker whose work email matches (workers:read)\n  rippling manager <worker-id>                    The worker's manager as a worker, or null (workers:read)\n  rippling reports-to <worker-id>                 Workers whose manager is that worker (workers:read)\n  rippling users | rippling user <id>             User accounts (workers:read)\n  rippling worker-changes [field=value ...]       Changes to worker records; filter=, order_by= (workers:read)\n  rippling departments | rippling teams | rippling locations | rippling titles | rippling levels | rippling employment-types   (org:read)\n  rippling custom-fields                          Custom field definitions (org:read)\n  rippling leave-requests [field=value ...] | rippling leave-balances | rippling leave-types   (leave:read)\n  rippling time-entries [field=value ...] | rippling time-cards [field=value ...]   (time:read)\n  rippling devices                                Managed devices (devices:read)\n  rippling activity-log [field=value ...]         Audit events of the last 90 days (activity-log:read)\n  rippling custom-objects | rippling records <object-api-name> [field=value ...]   (custom-objects:read)\n  rippling report <id> | rippling run-report <id> [json]   Report definitions and runs (reports:read, reports:write)\n  rippling get <path> [field=value ...]           Raw GET (one page)\n  rippling list <path> [field=value ...]          Raw GET, every page, as one array\n  rippling api <METHOD> <path> [json-body]        Raw call with an explicit method and JSON body\n"
  }
